course: dictionary
lesson: 1211
title: Planning with a budget
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A budget is a plan for how much money you will spend and how much you will save. «A town or city council has a limited budget, so spending money on one thing, like a library, means less for something else, like a swimming pool.» The words limited and means less are the clues: the budget is the money available, and it is not endless.
explain: To budget means to plan carefully how to spend money or time. «We need to budget for the school trip» means we must work out in advance what it will cost and save enough for it. If you are over budget, you have spent more than your plan allowed. If you are within budget, you have stayed under it.
explain: Budget can also be an adjective meaning cheap. «We stayed in a budget hotel by the sea.» The clue is that the family chose it to save money, so budget here means low in cost, not a plan.
fact: A budget is a plan for money: what comes in, what must go out on bills, and what is left for food, fun and saving.
fact: «Budget» can mean a plan, the money you have to spend, or the act of planning how to spend.
fact: «Budget» as an adjective means cheap, as in «a budget hotel».
fact: Phrases to know: «on a budget» means with little money, «over budget» means spent too much, and «within budget» means spent no more than planned.
fact: Families budget for food and bills, and schools and councils budget for things like libraries and pools.
exercise: «A town or city council has a limited budget.» What does budget mean here? | A swimming pool | A list of library books | A map of the town | *The money it has available to spend
exercise: Mum says, «We need to budget for the trip.» What does budget for mean? | *Plan and save the money the trip will cost | Run very fast to the coach | Eat lunch at home | Count the sheep in the field
exercise: Find and copy one word that means cheap in «We stayed in a budget hotel by the sea.» | *budget | stayed | hotel | sea
test: Ella's party will cost £20 but she only has a budget of £15. Is she within budget? | Yes, she has saved enough money | No, she has no party | *No, she is over budget | Yes, it is cheaper than a bus
test: What does it mean to budget your time? | Stop the clock | Waste time on games | *Plan carefully how to use your time | Sleep all day
exam: Which sentence uses budget to mean a plan for money? | We budget ran up the hill | The budget hotel had a big swimming pool | The room was budget and quiet | *Dad made a budget so the bills and food were all paid for
